{"version": 2, "width": 80, "height": 24, "timestamp": 1785112643, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/zsh", "TERM": null}, "title": "TraceMind — Full product tour"}
[0.011436, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[35m════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[35m ACT I — What is TraceMind?\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.011853, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[35m════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.019227, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m▸ The pitch\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mTraceMind is a local-only memory OS. Everything you're about to see runs on this laptop: real ONNX embeddings (BGE-small-384d), a SQLite graph, a JTMS truth-maintenance layer, ambient capture, tiered answers, and an MCP surface that plugs into Claude Code / Cursor / Goose. No cloud, no telemetry, ~/.tracemind/ is the whole footprint.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.026516, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind onboard --dry-run\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.050791, "o", "[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)\r\n"]
[5.051908, "o", "TraceMind onboarding\r\n  data dir: /tmp/tm-demo-tour\r\n  memory.db: not yet\r\n  model bge-384-v1.5          : missing (will download on first use)\r\n  model gliner-multi          : missing (will download on first use)\r\n  model mxbai-colbert         : missing (will download on first use)\r\n  entities in graph: 0\r\n  unconsolidated signals: 0\r\n"]
[5.052037, "o", "  onboarding marker: not written (dry run)\r\n"]
[8.075081, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[35m════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[35m ACT II — Ingestion, every shape\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.075386, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[35m════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.086793, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m▸ 1. Text ingest\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mPlain text goes through governance (regex PII + confidence gate) → heuristic NER (URLs, emails, dates, entity typing) → SQLite graph upsert → BGE embedding → immutable Trace event.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[12.09836, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind ingest 'Aaditya founded TraceMind in Palo Alto in July 2026. The company builds a local memory OS.'\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[13.124098, "o", "[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)\r\n"]
[13.759128, "o", "Ingested: \"Aaditya founded TraceMind in Palo Alto in July 2026. The company builds a local ...\"\r\n  Trace:    363bd893-b5bb-41f5-99f5-dc4f248f701f\r\n  Entities: 4\r\n    [Person] Aaditya\r\n    [Concept] TraceMind\r\n    [Location] Palo Alto\r\n    [Event] July 2026\r\n  Typed triples:\r\n    Aaditya -> Owns -> TraceMind\r\n  + 0 co-occurrence triples\r\n"]
[16.867408, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m▸ 2. URL ingest (browser-shaped)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mURLs get first-class treatment: raw URL becomes a Url entity AND the registrable domain becomes an Organization node. That means a query for 'FIFA' hits the graph directly, not just BGE similarity.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[18.879405, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m$ tracemind ingest \"https://www.fifa.com/tickets FIFA World Cup 2026 Tickets\"\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[19.511084, "o", "Ingested: \"https://www.fifa.com/tickets FIFA World Cup 2026 Tickets\"\r\n  Trace:    260b7a96-eb76-447e-a60e-9312db9692cf\r\n  Entities: 4\r\n    [Url] https://www.fifa.com/tickets\r\n    [Organization] fifa.com\r\n    [Event] FIFA World Cup 2026\r\n"]
[19.511254, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m$ tracemind ingest \"https://apnews.com/article/world-cup-2026-tickets Ticket resale prices for the 2026 World Cup\"\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[20.150748, "o", "Ingested: \"https://apnews.com/article/world-cup-2026-tickets Ticket resale prices for the 2...\"\r\n  Trace:    9a091809-c628-4ef6-8b84-98ee0123e7b2\r\n  Entities: 3\r\n    [Url] https://apnews.com/article/world-cup-2026-tickets\r\n    [Organization] apnews.com\r\n    [Event] World Cup\r\n"]
[20.150928, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m$ tracemind ingest \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.10997 GEPA Reflective Prompt Evolution\"\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[20.766759, "o", "Ingested: \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.10997 GEPA Reflective Prompt Evolution\"\r\n  Trace:    15c49501-857b-4955-94dc-94379e64ff1a\r\n  Entities: 3\r\n    [Url] https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.10997\r\n    [Organization] arxiv.org\r\n    [Organization] GEPA\r\n"]
[20.766895, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m$ tracemind ingest \"https://superlinked.com/vectorhub Vector Hub — Superlinked\"\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[21.382308, "o", "Ingested: \"https://superlinked.com/vectorhub Vector Hub — Superlinked\"\r\n  Trace:    c8c77d30-3892-49f7-88e8-b65121e8084a\r\n  Entities: 3\r\n    [Url] https://superlinked.com/vectorhub\r\n    [Organization] superlinked.com\r\n    [Product] Vector Hub\r\n"]
[23.391164, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m▸ 3. Bulk import — a directory of files\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mPoint 'tracemind import' at any folder. Each file becomes a Trace with content-addressed provenance. Ideal for onboarding an existing knowledge base.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[25.420981, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind import '/tmp/tm-demo-tour-import'\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[26.441623, "o", "[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)\r\n"]
[26.442629, "o", "Importing 3 files from /tmp/tm-demo-tour-import\r\n"]
[26.998922, "o", "  design-note.md (0 entities, 0 triples)\r\n"]
[27.066752, "o", "  investor-brief.md (2 entities, 0 triples)\r\n"]
[27.166692, "o", "  roadmap.md (3 entities, 0 triples)\r\n\r\nImport complete:\r\n  Imported: 3\r\n  Skipped:  0 (empty, non-UTF-8, or duplicate)\r\n  Errors:   0\r\n  Total:    0 KB processed\r\n"]
[30.259105, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m▸ 4. Ambient capture — opt-in per source\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mClipboard, shell history, screenshots, browser history, audio, calendar. Every source is opt-in and revocable. Default first-run: clipboard + shell on, everything else off. State persists to ~/.tracemind/capture_permissions.toml.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[32.267277, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind capture list\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[33.294747, "o", "[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)\r\n"]
[33.297272, "o", "on   clipboard   system clipboard (polled; high-entropy strings skipped)\r\non   shell       shell history (.zsh_history / .bash_history tailing)\r\non   notes       Apple Notes (macOS, AppleScript dump at backfill)\r\noff  screenshot  screenshots via OS hotkey (OCR + caption, raw image stays local)\r\noff  browser     browser bookmarklet / extension (page url, title, selection)\r\noff  audio       microphone via opt-in hotkey (Whisper-tiny, on-device)\r\noff  calendar    macOS EventKit / Google Calendar (read-only, oauth)\r\noff  pdf         PDFs in a watched folder (~/Downloads; text extracted on-device)\r\noff  email       email from a watched .eml drop folder (subject + body, stays local)\r\noff  photo       photo library EXIF (filename, capture time, GPS; image stays local)\r\n"]
[36.317276, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m▸ 5. Capture doctor — the honest permission story\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mReports which sources are actually reachable right now. macOS Safari needs Full Disk Access; the doctor tells you exactly what to grant. On builds with --features macos-screencapture, it also shows whether Vision-framework OCR is compiled in.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[38.329192, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind capture-doctor 2>&1 | head -25\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[39.353183, "o", "[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)\r\n"]
[39.402607, "o", "Capture doctor\r\n  [  OK] chrome: history readable\r\n  [PERM] safari: needs Full Disk Access — grant to the daemon binary in System Settings → Privacy & Security → Full Disk Access, then restart `tracemind-capture`\r\n  [  --] screenshot-ocr: unavailable (build with --features macos-screencapture on macOS + Xcode CLI Tools)\r\n\r\nTo grant Full Disk Access on macOS: open System Settings → Privacy & Security → Full Disk Access, click +, add `tracemind-capture` (and `tracemind` if you also run the CLI probe under launchd), then restart the daemon.\r\n"]
[42.424713, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[35m════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[35m ACT III — Memory backend\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[42.42506, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[35m════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[44.436355, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m▸ 6. Query — bandit-routed retrieval\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mThe query planner classifies the intent; a contextual bandit (LinUCB with 5 arms — narrow / medium / wide / deep / colbert) picks the retrieval width; results fuse dense (BGE) + BM25 lexical + recency + confidence via ComposedIndex, then ColBERT MaxSim reranks.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[46.447584, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind query 'world cup tickets'\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[47.471216, "o", "[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)\r\n"]
[47.731546, "o", "Query: 48e258de-b333-4555-8238-91413d059d9a\r\n"]
[47.731643, "o", "Answer (Extractive, 0ms):\r\nhttps://www.fifa.com/tickets FIFA World Cup 2026 Tickets\r\n"]
[47.731649, "o", "\r\nCitations: [1] signal:2, [2] signal:3, [3] signal:4, [4] entity:d569117a-43a1-4aba-9e1b-ab9323d81c00, [5] entity:863ca4d8-ae56-4550-8199-10bacda96ab8\r\n\r\n"]
[47.731662, "o", "  [Product] Tickets\r\n  [Event] FIFA World Cup 2026\r\n  [Url] https://www.fifa.com/tickets\r\n  [Organization] fifa.com\r\n  [Event] World Cup\r\n"]
[50.76261, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m▸ 7. Ask — tiered answer layer\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mExtractive Tier 0 always works. Tier 1 (Qwen 2.5 1.5B Q4 GGUF, ~900 MB) and Tier 2 (Apple FoundationModels on macOS 26+) are opt-in features. Answers ground on retrieved entities with citations — abstains rather than hallucinating.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[52.774664, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind ask 'where can I buy tickets for the 2026 World Cup?'\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[53.799743, "o", "[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)\r\n"]
[54.060393, "o", "https://www.fifa.com/tickets FIFA World Cup 2026 Tickets\r\n\r\n— tier-0 extractive • 0 ms • 5 citation(s)\r\n    [1] signal:2\r\n    [2] signal:3\r\n    [3] signal:7\r\n    [4] signal:1\r\n    [5] signal:8\r\n\r\n(hint: Tier-1 weights not present. `tracemind models pull` (~940 MB) unlocks prose answers.)\r\n"]
[57.091405, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m▸ 8. Quick recall — launcher target (X2/X8)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mSub-100ms, small top_k, no LLM. Bind this to a global shortcut in Raycast / Alfred: keystroke → the site you're thinking of, no chrome.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[59.102321, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind quick-recall 'reflective prompt' --top-k 3\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[60.124456, "o", "[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)\r\n"]
[60.24992, "o", "   1. [graph] GEPA\r\n   2. [graph] arxiv.org\r\n   3. [graph] TraceMind\r\n"]
[63.274814, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m▸ 9. Trace — immutable audit trail\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mEvery ingest + query produces a Trace (UUID, timestamp, content hash, entity IDs) written append-only to traces.jsonl. Ground truth for provenance and rollback.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[65.283804, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind trace --limit 6\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[66.306198, "o", "[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)\r\n"]
[66.307353, "o", "    Ingest 9a091809 | 3 entities, 0 triples | https://apnews.com/article/world-cup-2026-tickets Ticket res...\r\n    Ingest 15c49501 | 3 entities, 0 triples | https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.10997 GEPA Reflective Prompt Evol...\r\n    Ingest c8c77d30 | 3 entities, 0 triples | https://superlinked.com/vectorhub Vector Hub — Superlinked\r\n  Retrieve 9938c589 | 5 entities, 0 triples | world cup tickets\r\n           arm=0, latency=5ms\r\n  Retrieve 4497c63e | 16 entities, 1 triples | where can I buy tickets for the 2026 World Cup?\r\n           arm=0, latency=13ms\r\n  Retrieve d37aa867 | 5 entities, 1 triples | reflective prompt\r\n           arm=0, latency=4ms\r\n"]
[66.307454, "o", "\r\nUse --id <prefix> to see full detail for a trace.\r\n"]
[69.329394, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[35m════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[35m ACT IV — Graph features\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[69.329653, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[35m════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[71.337281, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m▸ 10. Backlinks — LM-1\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mEvery entity has a typed backlink panel: which entities link *to* it, with predicate + confidence. The graph is the primary UI, not vectors.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[74.011432, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind backlinks 575c637b-089a-4d62-a76e-a1526cbcb662\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[75.031678, "o", "[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)\r\n"]
[75.037923, "o", "Backlinks for [Organization] Anthropic (575c637b-089a-4d62-a76e-a1526cbcb662)\r\n  ← [Person] Alice — WorksAt _(conf 0.75)_\r\n  ← [Person] Carol — Owns _(conf 0.75)_\r\n  (2 total)\r\n"]
[78.060561, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m▸ 11. Contexts — decoupled by default (C-0)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mNamed namespaces. Every signal + triple inherits the active context_id at ingest time. Retrieval defaults to the active scope. The point: your local machine has MORE context blur than a browser — decoupling is the wedge.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[80.068241, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind context list\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[81.092163, "o", "[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)\r\n"]
[81.096588, "o", "no contexts yet — `tracemind context create <name>` to add one\r\n"]
[82.106853, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind context create work\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[83.131109, "o", "[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)\r\n"]
[83.139185, "o", "created context: work (8e77bee3-8dd7-4c63-b0a1-3e2808799dd9)\r\n"]
[84.149584, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind context list\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[85.17179, "o", "[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)\r\n"]
[85.177529, "o", "  work                     8e77bee3-8dd7-4c63-b0a1-3e2808799dd9\r\n"]
[88.199753, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m▸ 12. Memory Views — LM-11\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[88.200091, "o", "\u001b[2mSaved include/exclude splices of memory. Surgical control over which memories enter which session. Karpathy-style PKM: you own the graph.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[90.207804, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind view list\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[91.229958, "o", "[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)\r\n"]
[91.236102, "o", "no views yet — `tracemind view create <name>` to add one\r\n"]
[94.25563, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m▸ 13. Pending relations — LM-9\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mMid-confidence extractions land in a pending pool, waiting for confirmation. Nothing enters trusted memory without a decision path.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[96.266896, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind pending list\u001b[0m\r\n"]
