[139.927665, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[35m════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[35m ACT VII — Composition wedge (memory_context_for)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[139.927968, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[35m════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[141.940186, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m▸ 19. One primitive, every LLM host\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mThis is the innovation: memory_context_for(topic, budget) — a token-budgeted, cited context brief bindable to one keystroke in Claude Code / Cursor / Goose / Windsurf. Same primitive on the MCP surface. What follows is the CLI mirror.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[143.952182, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m$ ./target/release/tracemind context-for 'world cup tickets' --budget-tokens 500\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[144.977118, "o", "[tracemind] using bundled models from /Users/aadityasrivathsan/Desktop/agent_memory_system/target/release/models (bundle)\r\n"]
[145.112619, "o", "Topic: world cup tickets\r\n\r\nWhat we know:\r\n- [1] Tickets (custom(\"product\"))\r\n- [2] FIFA World Cup 2026 (event)\r\n- [3] https://www.fifa.com/tickets (url)\r\n- [4] fifa.com (organization)\r\n- [5] World Cup (event)\r\n\r\nRecent activity:\r\n- [6] https://www.fifa.com/tickets FIFA World Cup 2026 Tickets (ingest, 2026-07-27)\r\n- [7] https://apnews.com/article/world-cup-2026-tickets Ticket resale prices for the 2026 World Cup (ingest, 2026-07-27)\r\n- [8] FIFA World Cup 2026 final located in New Jersey (ingest, 2026-07-27)\r\n- [9] FIFA World Cup 2026 final located in Los Angeles (ingest, 2026-07-27)\r\n\r\nOpen commitments:\r\n- [10] buy Group Stage tickets before the price surge (Intent, due 2026-08-15)\r\n"]
[148.143489, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m▸ 20. Budget-aware truncation\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mTight budget → drops less-important sections and warns you. The brief always fits inside the budget it claims.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
